  "line": 801,
  "title": "Record a kept job as unconfirmed before its first process starts, and confirm it only from positive evidence",
  "detail": "Thank you: the discovery records fix the original sequence, and the daemon path and rollback compatibility were confirmed unchanged. Two gaps remain, found in review. (a) The child is spawned (proc.ts:801) before its discovery evidence is saved (proc.ts:822), and a preceding successful command may already have saved `confirmed: true` (client.ts:247). If the worker process dies between the spawn and the save, the next start trusts the old confirmation and removes the checkout without looking for the new child. (b) If building the discovery record fails (for example, boot-identity inspection at proc.ts:826 fails), this release saves `discoveries: [], confirmed: false`, and every later start stops with \"missing worker discovery evidence\" with no way out short of editing state by hand. Required: (1) when a job starts, before it spawns anything, save its kept entry as unconfirmed with what recovery needs to find its processes later: the job's scope marker or run id, the host boot identity when available, and its directories. Mark it confirmed only after the job's processes are confirmed gone. (2) At start, and on later attempts, an unconfirmed entry is confirmed either by a successful scan for that job's marker that finds no live processes, or by a different host boot identity than the one recorded (a reboot ended every earlier process). Only then are its directories removed. (3) Never refuse to start the worker because of an unconfirmed entry. Log it, keep its directories, retry confirmation on later heartbeats or starts, and keep running other jobs, whose directories are always new. Tests: worker death between spawn and save (simulate it by throwing after the spawn and before the save, then restarting), a failed boot-identity inspection followed by a restart (the worker starts, the directories are kept, a later successful scan removes them), and a changed boot identity confirming the entry."
 }
]
